                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Aesthetically the art was better in the first game.\n\nMy negative rating is due to these games requiring a ridiculous amount of grinding after completing all the puzzles in order to rack up another 700K coins for the final achievements.  As if this wasn't bad enough in the first game, the dev made the wonderful decision of adding an infinite tutorial loop to the first two puzzles in this game so that the least painful puzzles to grind out those 700K coins now have even more clicking required every time you repeat the puzzle.  The tutorial is never marked off as complete so it doesn't retrigger, there are no settings in the options menu to turn it off, and even deleting the tutorial files (there's over a dozen of the dang things) in the game files does not remove the tutorial prompt from every single time you launch puzzle 1 or 2.\n\nApparently the grind wasn't bad enough in the first game so the dev decided to double down on it for game 2.  Not worth your time to 100% this.",
